  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Quiet reading workspace",
    "overview": "This native Android interface uses Material 3 for the controls around an original technical document. Read and Operate are the guiding surface modes: the document occupies the available reading area, while the contents tree, search, history and settings support deliberate navigation. CHM Sharp is a workflow reference, not an asset source.\n\nThe app chrome is calm, compact and teal. The document retains its own HTML typography, colors, images and tables. These rules describe the implementation in `MainActivity.kt`, `ui/TocAdapter.kt`, `ui/SearchPanel.kt`, `ui/Icons.kt` and the two theme resources. This is a source-based record; Android visual, touch and assistive-technology verification remains outstanding because the emulator did not boot.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Native Material 3 controls with system typography.",
      "A white WebView canvas and unchanged document colors in both app themes.",
      "A real contents hierarchy with independent expansion and page actions.",
      "A phone drawer that becomes an adjustable persistent panel in wide windows."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Document Colors Rule",
        "body": "App theme changes affect chrome. Preserve the document's colors and disable WebView automatic darkening.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Reading Width Rule",
